#: ../../source/normalize-range_readme.md:39
msgid "wrap(min, max, value)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-range_readme.md:41
msgid ""
"Normalizes a values that \"wraps around\". For example, in a polar "
"coordinate system, 270˚ can also be represented as -90˚.  For wrapping "
"purposes we assume `max` is functionally equivalent to `min`, and that "
"`wrap(max + 1) === wrap(min + 1)`. Wrap always assumes that `min` is "
"*inclusive*, and `max` is *exclusive*. In other words, if `value === max`"
" the function will wrap it, and return `min`, but `min` will not be "
"wrapped."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-range_readme.md:54
msgid "You are not restricted to whole numbers, and ranges can be negative."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-range_readme.md:65
msgid "limit(min, max, value)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-range_readme.md:67
msgid ""
"Normalize the value by bringing it within the range. If `value` is "
"greater than `max`, `max` will be returned. If `value` is less than "
"`min`, `min` will be returned. Otherwise, `value` is returned unaltered. "
"Both ends of this range are *inclusive*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-range_readme.md:73
msgid "test(min, max, value, [minExclusive], [maxExclusive])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-range_readme.md:75
msgid ""
"Returns `true` if `value` is within the range, `false` otherwise. It "
"defaults to `inclusive` on both ends of the range, but that can be "
"changed by setting `minExclusive` and/or `maxExclusive` to a truthy "
"value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-range_readme.md:79
msgid "validate(min, max, value, [minExclusive], [maxExclusive])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-range_readme.md:81
msgid ""
"Returns `value` or throws an error if `value` is outside the specified "
"range."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-range_readme.md:83
msgid "name(min, max, value, [minExclusive], [maxExclusive])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-range_readme.md:85
msgid ""
"Returns a string representing this range in  [range "
"notation](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Interval_(mathematics)#Classification_of_intervals)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-range_readme.md:88
msgid "curry(min, max, [minExclusive], [maxExclusive])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-range_readme.md:90
msgid "Convenience method for currying all method arguments except `value`."
msgstr ""

